# Public hosting (free)

**Goal:** site works with the PC off, at $0.

Use **Render Free** (`render.yaml`):
1. User signs up at https://dashboard.render.com/register (GitHub, no card).
2. Push this project to GitHub.
3. Render → New → Blueprint → this repo.
4. Set `PUBLIC_URL` to `https://<service>.onrender.com`.

Free limitations: spin-down after ~15 min idle (~1 min wake). WebSocket traffic keeps it awake. Ephemeral disk — SQLite may reset on sleep/redeploy.

Do **not** promise the old Tunnelmole fixed URL as always-on/free.
Do **not** require paid Fly/Tunnelmole for the free path.
Local `npm start` + tunnel is only while the PC is on.
